    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "rebuilding... i dont know. how do you rebuild when the person who was supposed to do the building doesn't even exist anymore? the people i used to know, the life i had... it wasn't just a job, it was everything. it's not like a bad breakup or a lost investment. it's like the whole world just looks at me and sees a mistake. it feels like there's no path back from this. just a dead end.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is perfectly understandable to feel like the foundation of your life is gone, making the idea of \"rebuilding\" feel impossible right now. Healing isn't about instantly recreating the old self, but about slowly discovering who you are in this new, altered landscape. Focus on very small steps toward self-compassion, allowing yourself to simply exist without the immediate pressure to \"be\" something. Professionals can help you explore new anchors of self-worth outside of what you once achieved.",
      "source": "target",
